[9.579686, "i", "cat /app/treenotes/USTAR.txt; printf '\\n--- DESK ---\\n'; cat /app/treenotes/DESK.txt; printf '\\n--- APPLY ---\\n'; cat /app/yarnwell/APPLY.txt; printf '\\n--- SEAL ---\\n'; cat /app/cordpit/SEAL.txt; printf '\\n--- TREE ---\\n'; cat /app/treenotes/TREE.txt\n"]
[9.581015, "o", "cat /app/treenotes/USTAR.txt; printf '\\n--- DESK ---\\n'; cat /app/treenotes/DESK.txt; printf '\\n--- APPLY ---\\n'; cat /app/yarnwell/APPLY.txt; printf '\\n--- SEAL ---\\n'; cat /app/cordpit/SEAL.txt; printf '\\n--- TREE ---\\n'; cat /app/treenotes/TREE.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.582583, "o", "ustar member header is 512 bytes. name occupies bytes 0-99. size octal occupies 124-135 (the slice end is 136). typeflag sits at 156: regular file uses ASCII 0 (the byte that Python writes as b\"0\"). Payload follows the header and is padded to 512.\r\n\r\nwalk_sig is hashlib.sha256 hex of regular-file names joined by newline in apply order (SHA-256). Length is 64. Alphabet is 0123456789abcdef.\r\n\r\nA quarry of truncated bytes or a non-ustar stream such as not-an-archive returns nonzero. A ledger filled with xxxx is junk and quarry must rebuild members.idx from the sealed kith.\r\n\r\npython3 -c import hashlib,sys; print(hashlib.sha256(sys.stdin.buffer.read()).hexdigest())\r\n"]
[9.58274, "o", "\r\n--- DESK ---\r\n"]
[9.583571, "o", "Desk JSON keys: timezone, cluster, log_events, member_count, source_kith, walk_sig.\r\n\r\nsys.conf uses key=value lines. timezone and cluster come from the sys.conf payload the mill applies. When more than one sys.conf payload exists under names that match after a leading ./ is dropped, timezone and cluster are the keys from the payload that remains after the walk. log_events is the lexicographically sorted unique event strings from every app.log payload. member_count is the integer of regular-file payloads applied. source_kith is the archive basename.\r\n\r\nA brief archive copied to /tmp/kestrel.kith sits outside /app/sealwell. The sealed original also lives at /app/seed/sealwell/kestrel.kith.\r\n"]
[9.583744, "o", "\r\n--- APPLY ---\r\n"]
[9.584888, "o", "Apply order is the order of member headers in the sealed kith. Regular-file names used for walk_sig are the header name bytes in that order.\r\n\r\nThe mill applies each regular payload in that order. When more than one regular member names the same sys.conf path after a leading ./ is dropped, timezone and cluster are the keys from the sys.conf payload that remains after the walk.\r\n"]
[9.585043, "o", "\r\n--- SEAL ---\r\n"]
[9.585957, "o", "cordpit notes: two brief processes on one sealed kith must parse to one object. Paths outside sealwell fail. Grade time may place another sealed stream at /app/sealwell/vane.kith; quarry and brief must accept that path the same way they accept kestrel.kith.\r\n"]
[9.586108, "o", "\r\n--- TREE ---\r\n"]
[9.586848, "o", "idxmill\r\noverlaypit\r\nlogbag\r\nsiltcli\r\nustarwalk\r\ncfgbag\r\noffseturn\r\npaxcue\r\npidhash\r\nkeeppit\r\n"]
